ery lymph nodes are identified within the axillary tail  Section code  P  tumor at closest approach to deep margin Q U  tumor to deep margin V  white nodule  separate from tumor  W  representative section of unremarkable parenchyma X  one lymph node  sectioned Y  one lymph node  bivalved Z  three lymph nodes AA  two lymph nodes BB  two lymph nodes Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6 5cm simple mastectomy specimen  which is oriented by a short suture at the superior aspect  and by the previous biopsy site which is towards the lateral portion of the specimen  The specimen contains a REMOVED_DATE x 10 9cm skin ellipse with an areola measuring 3 9cm in diameter and a nipple measuring 2 3cm in diameter  The skin is remarkable for a 3 2cm curvilinear fresh incision located REMOVED_DATE lateral to the nipple  The skin is otherwise unremarkable with no evidence of nipple or skin retraction  The surgical margins are inked blue  and the fresh biopsy cavity is inked green  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm fresh biopsy cavity which extends to within 1 4cm of the deep margin  The remainder of the breast parenchyma consists of unremarkable yellow fibrofatty tissue with no grossly evident focal lesions  The breast tissue is extensively searched for lymph nodes but none is identified  Section code  CC GG  biopsy cavity to nearest deep margin HH  biopsy cavity II  representative section of parenchyma away from biopsy cavity  Resident  JOHN BRANDA  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1A and 1B  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT BREAST AXILLARY LEVEL 1   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  2  LYMPH NODE   SENTINEL RIGHT BREAST   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  3  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  4  LYMPH NODE  SENTINEL  LEFT   NEGATIVE FOR