ere developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  27 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 06 27 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast upper level  1 450  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm yellow tan lymph nodule which is bisected and one half is frozen as FX  1  and submitted as A  The remainder of the tissue is entirely submitted as B  Labeled  left breast upper level  1  REMOVED_CASE_ID   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm yellow tan  fibrofatty tissue which contains a single REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm lymph node which is bisected and one half is frozen as FX  2  and submitted as C  The remainder of the tissue is entirely submitted as D through E  Labeled  left breast lumpectomy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm yellow tan  fibrofatty tissue marked by a long stitch  lateral   short stitch  superior   Sectioning of the specimen reveals a ill defined  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  firm  white tan nodule in the superior lateral quadrant 0 5cm away from superior  anterior and deep margins  The remainder of the parenchyma is yellow  soft and unremarkable  F  Lateral margin en face  G  Superior margin  representative radial section  H  Anterior margin  representative radial sections  I  Deep margin  representative radial sections  J  Inferior margin  representative  Labeled  left breast  1 medial margin  are four fragments of yellow tan  fibrofatty tissue aggregating to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm which are inked in black  serially sectioned and entirely submitted as K M  No grossly