Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  03 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  03 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 19 38 CLINICAL DATA  Left modified radical mastectomy in a 45 year old female with a left breast mass which on mammogram was highly suggestive of carcinoma  FNA REMOVED_DATE showed isolated atypical cells  highly suggestive of carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL ADENOCARCINOMA  90    GRADE REMOVED_DATE  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED   REMOVED_DATE CM IN SIZE  AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  10    CRIBRIFORM AND SOLID TYPES  THE RESECTION MARGINS ARE NEGATIVE FOR CARCINOMA  2  TWENTY SEVEN OF TWENTY SEVEN LYMPH NODES ARE NEGATIVE  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 54                                                                                     HORMONE BINDING ASSAY Addendum     RESULTS OF HORMONE BINDING ASSAYS AS REPORTED BY DAVID T  MACLAUGHLIN  PhD   726  REMOVED_CASE_ID   estrogen receptor  Negative  progesterone receptor  Negative  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 18     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 unfixed breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 12 25 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  Left breast and axillary contents  is a 25 x 21 x 5cm left mastectomy specimen with attached axillary contents and a 23 x 8cm ellipse of skin containing unremarkable 1cm in diameter nipple  No lesions on the skin surface are identified  The deep surface is a thin unremarkable fibrous tissue overlying adipose tissue and is inked  Serial sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 6cm stellate firm white mass in the upper outer quadrant  5cm from the nipple and 2cm from the closest deep margin  A representative portion of the mass is frozen as frozen section  1 and saved frozen  Another piece is saved for estrogen receptors  The remainder of the breast tissue is predominantly adipose tissue with thin strands of fibrous tissue  No additional suspicious lesions are seen  The attached 7 x 5 x 2cm portion of axillary tail contains unremarkable lymph nodes up to 1 3cm in size  Section Code  A D  tumor  E  closest deep margin  F G  surrounding breast tissue  H M  lymph nodes  N  nipple  Resident  Daniel D  Koelliker  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  David Weissmann  M D  O R  Diagnosis by  Michael Pins  M D  O R  Consulting Pathologist s   Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD Lisa H  Lerner  MD                                                                             