ED_DATE CM FROM THE CLOSEST  NEW   STITCHED  MARGIN  BREAST  LEFT  ADDITIONAL   EXCISION FOR FROZEN SECTION  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The ductal carcinoma in situ nearly replaces the fragment  with extensive involvement of lobules   cancerization of lobules    it spans at least 1 8cm  and extends to the edges of the excision  Taken together with the other final slides and the immunostain results  all of the in situ tumor is of the ductal type  rather than lobular as suspected at the time of intraoperative consultation   GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and   left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 4cm pink orange  lobulated  hemorrhagic breast excision specimen  with a short suture indicating superior  a long suture indicating medial  and two stereotactic biopsy needles embedded in the tissue  The provided radiograft indicates calcification concentrated in the medial and lateral aspects of the specimen  The specimen is inked with respect to the medial  latera  long access as follows  anterior  blue  posterior  black  superior  green  inferior  yellow  The specimen is serially section from medial to lateral to reveal a pink  firm central parenchyma  with some surrounding yellow adipose tissue  as well as some peripherally located tan white  softer parenchyma  No well defined lesions or masses are identified  Representative sections of the specimens are submitted from medial to lateral in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   with  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  containing one half each of the same level  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final inferior margin   are two fragments of fibroadipose tissue  The larger specimen has two stitches on it that indicates the new margin  and it measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  the smaller portion is unoriented  and measures REMOVED_DATE x 1 0x 0 5cm  The larger specimen is inked black on the sutured side  and the smaller portion is inked black entirely  The larger portion is bisected and submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and the smaller portion is submitted entirely in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final medial   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm fragment of tan pink tissue with a suture on one side indicating the margin  The sutured side is inked black entirely and the specimen is submitted entirely in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast additional   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm unoriented fatty portion of soft tissue  that is bivalved and frozen entirely as frozen section  1  now resubmitted entirely in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION   1  SOFT TISSUE  LEFT BREAST ADDITIONAL   LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  Gross Dictation by Matthew M Johnson M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by John H Eichhorn M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The in situ tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The in situ tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum by Atul K Bhan M D   on REMOVED_DATE Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCIS