Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  30 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  30 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 18 49 CLINICAL DATA  Left brest cancaer  by FNA                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  100   GRADE REMOVED_DATE  MEASURING REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION  EXTENDING TO WITHIN REMOVED_DATE CM OF AN INKED RESECTION MARGIN  SEE NOTE  2  ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  SINGLE FOCUS  NOTE  Several foci suspicious for lymphatic invasion are identified  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   AXILLARY NODE DISSECTION  METASTATIC DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN EIGHT OF TWELVE LYMPH NODES WITH A SINGLE MICROSCOPIC FOCUS SUSPICIOUS FOR EXTRA  CAPSULAR EXTENSION   LYMPH NODE  AXILLA  LEVEL 1   FIBROADIPOSE TISSUE AND NERVE  NO LYMPHOID TISSUE IS IDENTIFIED  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  Andrea Flieder  MD Signed On  03 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 18 16                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 07 55 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  in a container  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  is a mastectomy consisting of breast measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm  ellipse of skin measuring REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm and axillary tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm  The nipple and areola appear grossly unremarkable  however  on the ellipse of skin approximately 1 0cm inferior to the nipple is a reddish brown area of ecchymosis measuring 3 0cm in greatest dimension  Immediately adjacent to this area of ecchymosis in the adipose tissue is a small well circumscribed  firm yellowish tan lesion measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  The lesion extends to approximately 0 1cm of an inked resection margin  In the remaining breast parenchyma there are multiple ill defined  firm  white nodules which are mainly in the superior medial quadrant  The axillary tissue is examined for lymph nodes  and twelve probable lymph nodes are identified  ranging in size from 0 5cm to 2 0cm  SECTION CODE  A  representative sections of overlying skin B D  representative sections of the lesion and deepest resection margin E H  contain representative sections of the nodular areas superior I  contains representative sections of five possible lymph nodes J  contains representative sections of three possible lymph nodes K  contains representative sections of three possible lymph nodes L  contains representative section from one possible lymph node  Submitted separately  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  level  1 lymph node material  is a single piece of adipose tissue  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm  The specimen is bisected and serially sectioned to reveal mainly adipose tissue  No lymph nodes are identified  The specimen is submitted in its entirety in M and N  Resident  KEITH KWAN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  COMP  BREAST HEALTH CENTER REPORTS TO  Kenneth Kenji Tanabe  M D  Kenneth Kenji Tanabe  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT  PART B  AXILLARY NODE  LEFT    report_end  , Negative.
