Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  13 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  13 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 11 13 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  2    TWO FOCI  REMOVED_DATE AND REMOVED_DATE CM  WELL TO MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE I II III   EACH FOCUS REMOVED_DATE CM FROM AN INKED SURFACE  SEE NOTE  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  98    EXTENSIVE  FORMING A REMOVED_DATE CM MASS  SOLID  CRIBRIFORM AND FOCALLY COMEDO TYPES WITH ASSOCIATED CALCIFICATIONS  PRESENT AT SEVERAL INKED SURFACES  SEE NOTE  3  INTRADUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  FOCAL  4  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH APOCRINE METAPLASIA  INTRALOBULAR FIBROSIS AND SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  5  MONCKEBERG S MEDIAL CALCIFIC SCLEROSIS  NOTE  Blood vascular and lymphatic invasion is not seen  The ductal carcinoma in situ forms a dominant mass of 1 5cm  and is also present focally throughout the entire  all eleven slides  specimen  The two foci of invasive ductal carcinoma are present within the main mass of ductal carcinoma in situ  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  ER and PR will be reported in an addendum  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  17 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 15 48                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  21 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 08 32 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm tan  fibrofatty fragment of breast tissue  Inked and sectioned to reveal a 1 5cm nodule  A representative section was frozen as FX  1 and saved frozen  The remaining tissue is submitted entirely in cassette A through K  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  RIGHT BREAST MASS  DUCTAL CARCINOMA  ONLY DCIS IS IDENTIFIED ON THE FROZEN SECTION SLIDE  PROBABLY APOCRINE CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  CHIN LEE WU  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Ben Zion Pilch  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Positive.
