E CARCINOMA  Invasive carcinoma extends to   0 1cm from the posterior margin of the specimen along a broad front  LOCATION OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Within the region of the mass  GRADE OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  1  MARGIN OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater  STAINS FOR RECEPTORS  Requested on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   NOTE  Immunohistochemical stains for e cadherin performed on slides  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  show positive staining in the invasive carcinoma and confirm the diagnosis of invasive ductal carcinoma  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are 7 containers which are  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  sentinel node left axilla   REMOVED_CASE_ID    is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm tan pink lymph node  which is bisected and entirely submitted for frozen section as FX 1  now as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh  labeled  left breast lumpectomy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 2cm portion of tan red fibrofatty tissue  with a short black stitch designating the superior margin  and a long black stitch designating the lateral margin  The posterior margin is inked black  the anterior blue  the superior green  and the inferior yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm indurated gray white mass  with associated hemorrhage  comes to 0 2cm of the posterior margin  0 3cm of the superior margin  0 6cm of the inferior margin  0 5cm of the anterior margin  1 5cm of the lateral margin  and 2 0cm of the medial margin  Peripherally noted along the lateral aspect of the mass is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm cavity  consistent with previous biopsy site  The remaining cut surface displays focally dense gray white fibrous tissue  with no other discrete lesions or other gross abnormalities  Representative sections are submitted fro