 this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 07 33 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast lump   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm a tan to yellow  striated  gritty  firm  piece of tissue  A representative section is frozen as FX 1 and saved frozen  representative sections of the remaining tissue is in A through J  including tumor closest to the margin  Also present is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm skin ellipse  The skin ellipse is in K  Resident  FANG FANG  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  RIGHT BREAST  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  JAMES J  TIESINGA  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Peter Hedberg  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST LUMP   report_end  , Positive.
